            "Chang, Aeschbach, Duffy & Czeisler (2015), PNAS (12 adults, tightly controlled)", Evidence.GOOD),
        Lesson("e-gray", Topic.EVIDENCE, "Grayscale makes the feed duller",
            "In a randomized field experiment, switching phones to grayscale cut screen time right away, more than setting time limits did. Another study found grayscale gave people more sense of control and less stress, though unlock counts didn't change. It's a tool for less use, not a brain upgrade.",
