        Lesson("e-presence", Topic.EVIDENCE, "Does a phone on the desk drain your brain?",
            "A famous 2017 study from UT Austin, the one often quoted in talks, said yes, even with the phone switched off. Direct replications didn't find the effect, and two meta-analyses disagree: one found a small cost, a larger one found no overall effect. What's clearer is that a phone within reach gets picked up more.",
            "Out of reach beats willpower: another room if you can, a bag if you can't.",
