        Lesson("e-table", Topic.EVIDENCE, "A phone on the table makes talks shallower",
            "In a field study, 100 pairs of people talked in cafés for ten minutes. When either person put a phone on the table or held one, they rated the conversation as less fulfilling and felt less empathy from their partner, most of all between close friends. The effect was modest, but real.",
            "With people you care about, put the phone in a bag or pocket, not on the table.",
            "Misra, Cheng, Genevie & Yuan (2016), Environment and Behavior", Evidence.GOOD),
        Lesson("e-shorts", Topic.EVIDENCE, "Short videos make you forget your plans",
            "In an experiment with 60 people, those who watched TikTok-style short videos during a break were much worse afterwards at remembering to carry out an action they had planned. Twitter, YouTube and simply resting didn't have that effect. Rapid switching between short clips seems to be the problem.",
            "If you need to remember something later, skip short-video feeds in between.",
