            "A large 2025 review pooled studies of short-form video (TikTok, Reels, Shorts). Heavier use went along with weaker attention and self-control, and with more stress and anxiety. But most of the studies were snapshots taken at one moment, so they can't say whether short videos cause these problems or whether people who already struggle watch more. Probably some of both.",
