            "In studies by psychologist Gabriele Oettingen, people who fantasized most positively about a goal (a new job, losing weight, a crush) did worse at reaching it. Picturing the outcome as already done seems to relax you, as if you'd arrived: in one experiment, positive fantasies lowered people's energy, measured by blood pressure.",
            "Enjoy the dream for a moment, then name the first thing inside you that could get in the way.",
