            "You can't detox from dopamine: your brain makes it all the time, and you need it to move, learn and want anything at all. A day of 'no stimulation' doesn't reset it. What the trend gets right is older and plainer: take away the cues that trigger a habit (the app on the first screen, the phone by the bed) and the urge comes less often. Psychologists call that stimulus control.",
            "Remove one cue today instead of fasting from everything.",
            "Berridge & Robinson (2016), American Psychologist; Cameron Sepah, who coined 'dopamine fasting', describes it as stimulus control from CBT", Evidence.GOOD),
